refsect1.para:
Software packages install their unit specification files in
@INSTALLCONFIGDIR@ as described below.
@LOCALCONFIGDIR@ is the local override
directory. vera reads a unit file from
@LOCALCONFIGDIR@ if one exists instead of the
original one from @INSTALLCONFIGDIR@.
This allows modifying or adjusting the software package's unit
specification file without touching the original one.

@OVERRIDECONFIGDIR@ gets used for tracking
masked and enabled units, and does not normally need any manual
intervention.

note.para:
vera ignores unit specification files in
@LOCALCONFIGDIR@ unless the original
one is installed in
@INSTALLCONFIGDIR@.
@LOCALCONFIGDIR@ overrides, and does not
supplement, the contents of
@INSTALLCONFIGDIR@.

listitem.para:
Each runlevel (see
vera.runlevels 8
) has a corresponding system/name. Installing a unit specification for a specific runlevel is nothing more than defining enabled: system/name in its specification file, for example:

note.para:
The switch command (see
vera.runlevels 8
) immediately updates the advertised runlevels. Commands started to stop units from the previous runlevel see the new runlevel in the RUNLEVEL environment variable.
